<sect1 id="compare_floats_8h_1motivation">
<title>Motivation</title><para>&quot;NaClSublimationCurve&quot; is legacy code from Thomas Driesner&apos;s developments for the H2O-NaCl system, and computes the vapor pressure at sublimation (NaCl vapor / halite phase transition). It can be used standalone if only this information is needed. Otherwise, it is only used in the CSMP++ context for building accurate lookup tables for the H2O-NaCl system, which are significantly faster if the full system properties are needed.</para>
<para>Details of the underlying formulation can be found in</para>
<para>Driesner T. and Heinrich C.A. (2007): The system H2O-NaCl. Part I: Correlation formulae for phase relations in temperature-pressure-molefraction space from 0 to 1000oC, 0 to 5000 bar, and 0 to 1 XNaCl. Geochimica et Cosmochimica Acta 71, 4880-4901.</para>
</sect1>
<sect1 id="classcsmp_1_1_upwind_control_visitor_1usage">
<title>Usage</title><para>Construct an instance of &quot;NaClSublimationCurve&quot; with the temperature (in C) as constructor argument. &quot;NaClSublimationCurve&quot; has an internal mechanism to make sure that it always uses the current value of that temperature as they exist in your code. Public member names should be self-explanatory, I hope.</para>
<para><programlisting><codeline><highlight class="keywordtype">double</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>t(somevalue);<sp/></highlight><highlight class="comment">//<sp/>temperature<sp/>[C]<sp/>in<sp/>user&apos;s<sp/>application</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">...</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">NaClSublimationCurve<sp/>naclboil(t);<sp/></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">...</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight><highlight class="comment">//<sp/>here,<sp/>t<sp/>may<sp/>be<sp/>updated</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">...</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">cout<sp/>&lt;&lt;<sp/></highlight><highlight class="stringliteral">&quot;new<sp/>NaCl<sp/>sublimation<sp/>pressure:<sp/>&quot;</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>&lt;&lt;<sp/>naclboil.VaporPressure()<sp/>&lt;&lt;<sp/></highlight><highlight class="stringliteral">&quot;Pa\n&quot;</highlight><highlight class="normal">;<sp/></highlight><highlight class="comment">//<sp/>compute<sp/>and<sp/>output<sp/>vapor<sp/>pressure<sp/>on<sp/>sublimation<sp/>curve<sp/>[Pa]<sp/>for<sp/>new<sp/>temperature</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting></para>
</sect1>
<sect1 id="classcsmp_1_1_upwind_control_visitor_1issues">
<title>Known issues</title><para>The underlying equations are valid only in a restricted temperature-pressure range; range checking and error handling has not yet been implemented</para>
</sect1>
<sect1 id="compare_floats_8h_1testing">
<title>Testing</title><para>tested against CSP version (ok), which in turn was tested in the period before publication in 2007, prior to writing this documentation, no details are available anymore </para>
</sect1>
